From 04b9dd38c0a9b163cfea6130798f5c4bc264daf1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Date: Sat, 30 May 2026 15:18:24 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] freedreno: A22X route deadlock-prone GMEM batches to sysmem
 (FBO read-back OR >=25 draws on multi-tile FB)

On A22X (Adreno 220/225) the EDRAM back-end deadlocks for two GMEM-tile
batch classes:

  (a) FBO read-back / multi-pass compositing -- batch->restore != 0
      (e.g. glmark2 desktop:effect=blur w=4 composite batches).
  (b) High aggregate work on multi-tile FBOs -- pixels >= 512x512 AND
      num_draws >= 25 (e.g. glmark2 desktop:effect=shadow w=4).

Empirical per-batch DIAG instrumentation of the webOS surface-manager
compositor shows its heaviest steady-state batches are num_draws=13 on
1024x768 -- below the chosen threshold of 25. Earlier shipping of this
patch used num_draws >= 10 which (correctly) routed those compositor
batches to sysmem, but the sysmem path has a different intermittent
failure mode for surface-manager's specific draw shape that the GMEM
path handles cleanly. So we tune the threshold high enough to skip
surface-manager normal work while still catching the actually-broken
shadow class.

Validated 2026-05-30 across the test matrix:

  surface-manager:                          GMEM (max num_draws=13)
                                            0 hangchecks/90s
  jellyfish (num_draws=2):                  GMEM, 12 fps
  glmark2 build/shading/bump (num_draws=1): GMEM, --validate Success
  binner_test heavy (small batches):        GMEM
  glmark2 desktop:blur w=4 (restore=0x4):   sysmem via restore, 21 fps
  glmark2 desktop:shadow w=4 (num_draws=25-50): sysmem via draws+area
                                            71 fps (was 26 + hang)

Requires the sysmem-prep correctness fixes (RB_DEPTH_INFO emit + skip
HW fast-clear under sysmem; see memory/project_a220_sysmem_path_fixed)
to be in place, otherwise auto-routed batches would render garbage.

FD_MESA_DEBUG=gmem forces GMEM for debug; FD_MESA_DEBUG=sysmem forces
sysmem unconditionally.

Upstream-Status: Pending

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 .../drivers/freedreno/freedreno_gmem.c        | 41 +++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 41 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/gallium/drivers/freedreno/freedreno_gmem.c b/src/gallium/drivers/freedreno/freedreno_gmem.c
index a5ea50ad9eb..0365debdf52 100644
--- a/src/gallium/drivers/freedreno/freedreno_gmem.c
+++ b/src/gallium/drivers/freedreno/freedreno_gmem.c
@@ -23,6 +23,7 @@
 #include "freedreno_gmem.h"
 #include "freedreno_query_hw.h"
 #include "freedreno_resource.h"
+#include "freedreno_screen.h"
 #include "freedreno_tracepoints.h"
 #include "freedreno_util.h"
 
@@ -780,6 +781,46 @@ fd_gmem_render_tiles(struct fd_batch *batch)
       if ((pfb->nr_cbufs == 0) && !pfb->zsbuf.texture) {
          sysmem = true;
       }
+
+      /* A22X (Adreno 220/225) GMEM-deadlock heuristic.
+       *
+       * On A22X the EDRAM back-end deadlocks (RBBM_STATUS=0xc4010310, all of
+       * GUI+RB+VGT+CP_NRT busy + CP cmd FIFO 1/16 free, no progress) on two
+       * classes of GMEM-tile batches:
+       *
+       *   (a) FBO read-back / multi-pass compositing: batch->restore != 0
+       *       (some attachment must be restored from sysmem at tile-load
+       *       because this batch did not fully clear it). Catches glmark2
+       *       desktop:effect=blur w=4 ping-pong composite batches.
+       *   (b) High aggregate work on multi-tile FBOs: pixels >= 512*512 AND
+       *       num_draws >= 25. The threshold is empirically tuned: webOS
+       *       surface-manager's heaviest steady-state batches are
+       *       num_draws=13 on 1024x768, while glmark2 desktop:effect=shadow
+       *       w=4 produces num_draws=25-50 batches that DO hit the deadlock.
+       *
+       * Both classes are unavoidable at the cmdstream level: bounded
+       * submission and KGSL-pattern sync are both falsified (see
+       * memory/project_a220_blur_hang_cmdstream_analysis). KGSL ships A220
+       * with bins=0 universally (see memory/reference_kgsl_vs_freedreno_heavy_scene).
+       *
+       * FD_MESA_DEBUG=gmem forces GMEM for debug; FD_MESA_DEBUG=sysmem
+       * forces sysmem unconditionally.
+       *
+       * Validated 2026-05-30:
+       *   surface-manager (max num_draws=13 / 1024x768):   GMEM, 0 hangs/90s
+       *   jellyfish (1024x768, num_draws=2):               GMEM, 12 fps
+       *   glmark2 build/shading/bump (num_draws=1):        GMEM, Success
+       *   binner_test heavy (256x256 batches, num_draws=1): GMEM
+       *   glmark2 desktop:blur w=4 (1024x768, restore=0x4): sysmem via restore, 21 fps
+       *   glmark2 desktop:shadow w=4 (1024x768, num_draws=25-50): sysmem via draws+area, 71 fps
+       */
+      if (is_a22x(ctx->screen) && !FD_DBG(GMEM)) {
+         const unsigned pixels = pfb->width * pfb->height;
+         if (batch->restore ||
+             (pixels >= 512 * 512 && batch->num_draws >= 25)) {
+            sysmem = true;
+         }
+      }
    }
 
    if (FD_DBG(SYSMEM))
-- 
